1
00:00:00.423 --> 00:00:04.479
Unit sixteen. Intro to Blockchain Basics!

2
00:00:05.437 --> 00:00:10.264
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:10.314 --> 00:00:13.950
Hi, Mr. Daniel! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.538
Today we learn about Intro to Blockchain Basics. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.697 --> 00:00:23.748
Blockchain. Say it with me. Blockchain!

6
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.694
Distributed ledger. Say it with me. Distributed ledger!

7
00:00:35.211 --> 00:00:39.678
Decentralization. Say it with me. Decentralization!

8
00:00:43.153 --> 00:00:46.450
Block. Say it with me. Block!

9
00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:55.046
Cryptographic hash. Say it with me. Cryptographic hash!

10
00:00:58.448 --> 00:01:03.440
Consensus mechanism. Say it with me. Consensus mechanism!

11
00:01:06.944 --> 00:01:11.494
Transparent record. Say it with me. Transparent record!

12
00:01:15.047 --> 00:01:18.764
Immutable. Say it with me. Immutable!

13
00:01:22.235 --> 00:01:33.409
Blockchain is a distributed ledger built on decentralization. Each block uses a cryptographic hash, and a consensus mechanism creates a transparent, immutable record.

14
00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:36.953
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:37.691 --> 00:01:42.904
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:42.954 --> 00:01:44.471
Decentralization!

17
00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:50.976
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:51.026 --> 00:01:52.730
Transparent record!

19
00:01:53.625 --> 00:02:03.023
Did you know? Once information is recorded on most blockchains, it becomes extremely difficult to alter or delete, which is why it's called 'immutable'!

20
00:02:03.073 --> 00:02:05.272
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:17.633
Think and answer. Why might 'decentralization' be considered both a strength and a challenge for blockchain technology?

22
00:02:17.683 --> 00:02:18.833
Great answer!

23
00:02:20.019 --> 00:02:25.054
